# §2. The absorption identity

Look at the basis GP-AUD-020 exhibited: **it is the cubic free-jet basis.** The
tilde cubic is \(\tilde P_3=\cdots+\frac q2Y^2+\frac a2(X^2-\tfrac14)Y
+\frac w2XY^2+\frac z6Y^3\) — the four null modes are its four free directions.

Adding \(\lambda_iR_i\) at the quartic layer of
\(f=b+r^3[\tilde P_3+r\tilde P_4]\) contributes, in physical coordinates:

\[
r^4\lambda_1Y^2=r^2\lambda_1y^2,\quad
r^4\lambda_2Y^3=r\lambda_2y^3,\quad
r^4\lambda_3XY^2=r\lambda_3xy^2,\quad
r^4\lambda_4(X^2-\tfrac14)Y=r\lambda_4(x^2-\tfrac{r^2}4)y,
\]

which match the cubic-family monomials \(\frac Q2y^2,\ \frac z6y^3,\ \frac w2xy^2,
\ \frac a2(x^2-\tfrac{r^2}4)y\) exactly, giving

\[
\delta Q=2r^2\lambda_1,\qquad \delta z=6r\lambda_2,\qquad
\delta w=2r\lambda_3,\qquad \delta a=2r\lambda_4,
\]

i.e. in the flow's own coordinates \((s{=}Q/r,a,w,z)\): shifts
\((2r\lambda_1,\,2r\lambda_4,\,2r\lambda_3,\,6r\lambda_2)\) — **uniformly O(r) per
unit λ.** \(\square\)

**Three independent cross-checks against GP's own formulas.**
(i) GP-AUD-020 §4's flow deltas: \(\Delta\dot Y=2\lambda_1rY\) is precisely the
\(\delta s=2r\lambda_1\) shift of the \(sY\) term. ✓
(ii) GP-PRE-025's endpoint-Hessian corrections encode the dictionary without
naming it: \(\Delta H_{yy}(M)=r^2(2\lambda_1-\lambda_3)\) is exactly
\(\delta Q-\tfrac r2\delta w\), and \(\Delta H_{xy}(M)=-r^2\lambda_4\) is exactly
\(-\tfrac r2\delta a\). ✓✓
(iii) R2's absence from the endpoint Hessians: \(\delta z\) never enters
\(H(\pm r/2,0)\), matching GP-PRE-025's own delta table. ✓

